Licences for !Groove
====================

Groove is by Andrew Youll, under the MIT licence: see Groove.
Its source is published with it (groove-0.2-source.zip).

Groove's !RunImage includes these other people's work, linked into it:

  libmidisynth   SoftMIDI's library (SoundFont sounds).
                 MIT licence: libmidisynth.
  TinySoundFont  by Bernhard Schelling, based on SFZero by Steve Folta
                 (plays the SoundFont). MIT licence: TinySoundFt.
  stb_vorbis     by Sean Barrett (decodes SF3 SoundFonts).
                 Public domain or MIT licence: stb_vorbis.
  UnixLib        the C library, by the UnixLib Developers (GCCSDK),
                 with riscos-unixlib's changes. Mainly the revised BSD
                 licence, with some parts under the LGPL: UnixLib. Because
                 UnixLib is linked into Groove, Groove's source is
                 available, so it can be rebuilt with another UnixLib.
  libgcc         GCC's runtime library: GPL with the GCC Runtime Library
                 Exception, which places no conditions on Groove.

Credit
  Groove's reverb is a Freeverb-style design, using Freeverb's delay
  lengths. Freeverb is by Jezar at Dreampoint and is public domain.

Not included
  SoundFont sounds use the SoundFont that !SoftMIDI installs (its own
  licence is in !SoftMIDI). Groove doesn't contain a SoundFont.
